{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"pages":{"2118":{"pageid":2118,"ns":0,"title":"Bullseye","revisions":[{"revid":56920,"parentid":55673,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bullseye\n|Image       = Blue-Bullseye.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;11) damage.<br>Apply (2;3) {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Lock-On\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Lock-On\n|Image        = Icon LockOn.png\n|Description  = Receives 50% more damage from {{KW|Orb|Orbs}} for X turns.\n|Type         = Debuff\n|Stacks       = Duration\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|InteractsWith = Orb\n}}\n{{C|Bullseye}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* In general, additive effects are applied before multiplicative ones. If a damaging Orb is improved by {{BD|Focus}} and then damages an enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}, the {{BD|Focus}} will be added before the 50% increase from {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Lock-On}} improves the damage of all {{KW|Lightning}} and {{KW|Dark}} Orb sources.\n* {{C|Electrodynamics}} is helpful in multi enemy combats for making sure the damage from {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hits the enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} apply before {{BD|Lock-On}}, allowing for large damage output: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}.\n* In addition to general Orb sources, cards that can manually {{KW|Evoke}} Orbs can be very useful for dealing damage with {{BD|Lock-On}}: {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, {{C|Multi-Cast}}\n** {{C|Fission}} is a particular powerful option for this, allowing all of your damaging Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} while the [[Debuff]] is active.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, reducing the damage output of your Orbs.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Bullseye is the only source in the game of {{BD|Lock-On}}. It is not unique in this regard, as {{BD|Mark}} has {{C|Pressure Points}} as its only source.\n* The art of Bullseye appears to be a {{KW|Lightning}} and {{KW|Dark}} Orb being fired at [[Donu]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Bullseye card buffed. Lock-On 1 -> 2.\n** Bullseye+ card buffed. Damage 10 -> 11.\n\n* '''Switch Version 1.02'''\n** Fixed Lock-On bug\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Lock-On Power no longer incorrectly has the focused targeting effect.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Lock-On card reworked.\n** Lock-On card renamed -> Bullseye.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1906":{"pageid":1906,"ns":0,"title":"Corruption","revisions":[{"revid":56614,"parentid":56433,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Corruption\n| Image       = Red-Corruption.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 3\n| CostPlus    = 2\n| Description = Skills cost 0.<br>Whenever you play a Skill, {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n| PowerGives = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Corruption\n| Image        = Icon Corruption.png\n| Description  = {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} cost 0. Whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Does not stack\n| BetweenTurns = \n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{C|Corruption}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Corruption}}, which makes all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} have an {{Icon|RE}}-cost of 0, and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} them after they are played. As {{BD|Corruption}} does not stack, copies of {{C|Corruption}} played after the first have no additional effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}}, most notably {{C|Dark Embrace}}, as it allows you to keep drawing new {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}}, and {{R|Dead Branch}}, as it allows you to keep playing any {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} you draw or create. \n\n=== Neutral ===\n* With {{BD|Corruption}}, when randomizing the '''Energy''' {{Icon|RE}}-cost of cards through {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}}, the cost of all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards will remain 0.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** (Undocumented) Rarity changed from Uncommon to Rare.\n\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Confusion and Corruption cards utilize improved hooks.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}